.TH "NOTIFICATION.BADGE" "3JS" "October 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Notification.badge \- Notification: badge property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]badge\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]Notification\f[R] interface returns a string containing the URL of
a small icon representing the web application itself.
The badge is used by the platform when there is not enough space to
display the full notification \(em for example, in a status bar.
On Android, the badge should accommodate up to 4x display resolution
(about 96×96px), and the image will be automatically masked to a
monochrome silhouette.
.PP
See Notifications with different images for a comparison of the three
image options.
.SH VALUE
A string containing a URL.
